mac80211: debug -- count ieee80211_rx_irqsafe enqueues

Companion to DEBUG-mac80211-tasklet-counters.patch (read that header first).
Increments the same-module global mac80211_dbg_frames_queued on every enqueue,
so /proc/mac80211_tasklet_debug can show whether frames keep arriving from
this path after the hardware interrupt line has gone silent.

Not intended to stay in the tree once the storm is identified.

--- a/net/mac80211/rx.c
+++ b/net/mac80211/rx.c
@@ -5495,12 +5495,15 @@
 
 /* This is a version of the rx handler that can be called from hard irq
  * context. Post the skb on the queue and schedule the tasklet */
+extern unsigned long mac80211_dbg_frames_queued; /* debug, issue #99 */
+
 void ieee80211_rx_irqsafe(struct ieee80211_hw *hw, struct sk_buff *skb)
 {
 	struct ieee80211_local *local = hw_to_local(hw);
 
 	BUILD_BUG_ON(sizeof(struct ieee80211_rx_status) > sizeof(skb->cb));
 
+	mac80211_dbg_frames_queued++;
 	skb->pkt_type = IEEE80211_RX_MSG;
 	skb_queue_tail(&local->skb_queue, skb);
 	tasklet_schedule(&local->tasklet);
